The '''Koenigsegg Gemera''' is a limited production four-seat [[plug-in hybrid]] [[grand tourer]] (or 2-door [[sports saloon]]) manufactured by the Swedish automobile manufacturer [[Koenigsegg]]. It was unveiled on 3 March 2020 at an online broadcast by Koenigsegg at the cancelled [[Geneva Motor Show]].<ref name=":2">{{cite news |last1=Wilkinson |first1=Luke |title=New 1,700bhp Koenigsegg Gemera launched |url=https://www.autoexpress.co.uk/geneva-motor-show/351797/new-1700bhp-koenigsegg-gemera-launched |accessdate=3 March 2020 |work=Auto Express |date=3 March 2020 |language=en}}</ref><ref name=":3">{{cite news |last1=Pattni |first1=Vijay |title=The Koenigsegg Gemera is a 1,700bhp four-seat 'Mega GT' |url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/geneva-motor-show-2020/koenigsegg-gemera-1700bhp-four-seat-mega-gt |accessdate=3 March 2020 |work=Top Gear |date=3 March 2020 |language=en}}</ref> The name is a combination of the Swedish words ''ge'' and ''mera'', which translate to "give more".<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.koenigseggflorida.com/gemera/ |title=Gemera {{!}} Koenigsegg Florida |access-date=2026-01-08}}</ref>

